						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16578#msg16578"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16578#msg16578">Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2742 on:</b> April 21, 2005, 09:24:13 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I personally felt they needed to make the Msha&#039;s harder, and it would have eliminated much of the debate. Just increasing thier Melee DPS would have solved it in my opinion. Make it so that even under optimal skill levels and gear taken into consideration, it would still take a minimum of 3 groups to kill one, 4-5 for lesser skilled/equipt players. The only reason these were such a contested thing, is they can be single grouped so easily at later levels of gear and skill.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
